From f17dcb9741131f6f6d2fd12a65ccf391ce157986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:11:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FlySync: settings at flyweb://settings/flysync, no Brave Sync
 remnants, orange pills

- The sync settings move from /braveSync[/setup] to /flysync[/setup]
  (kBraveSyncPath, kBraveSyncSetupPath, the routes, the menu link). Old
  URLs (bookmarks, history) are rewritten in addBraveRoutes() before the
  Router reads the location; flyweb://sync still lands on the page.
- 27 strings of the page lose "Sync"/"FlyWeb Sync" and "device":
  FlySync and "computer" ("equipo"). New grit ids; es and es-419 get
  new translations; the other languages keep their existing translation
  moved to the new id, so none falls back to English.
- Every message of the account page (warnings, errors, states, weak
  password) is an orange pill (#FF9900, the FlyWeb notices' orange) with
  black text in light and dark mode, without the red border or red
  text. Buttons on it: white with black text, the main one black with
  white text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2hjxRPyuefYzGRoZRk
